// Pyright config. NOTE: pyright accepts // comments here but NOT a "_comment" key -
// an unrecognised setting makes it exit non-zero with
//   Config contains unrecognized setting "_comment"
// on every run, which is why this prose is in comments. The file must also stay
// BOM-free: a UTF-8 BOM makes pyright fail to parse it outright.
//
// typeCheckingMode is pinned to pyright's default, so adding this file changes
// nothing about how the existing modules are analysed - it exists only for
// extraPaths.
//
// tests/ imports build_api_reference from scripts/ via a runtime sys.path.insert
// (the same trick that lets the offline suite read ENTITIES without importing
// mcp_server). Pyright cannot follow that, so it is told directly rather than
// silenced with a per-import type: ignore.
{
  "typeCheckingMode": "standard",
  "extraPaths": ["scripts"]
}
